From 465b0a7d309724f8a182c36688440785b7af66dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 24bit192kHz <24bit192khz@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:41:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] soc/intel/skylake: Add the GbE ACPI device

Include the common GbE ACPI device. It carries the PME wake, so Wake-on-
LAN appears in /proc/acpi/wakeup as on the vendor firmware.

TEST=T480: GLAN listed in /proc/acpi/wakeup (S4).

Change-Id: I84a7e3b6171701aeb57dfc9d3acbd8e0e46a130e
Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: 24bit192kHz <24bit192khz@proton.me>
---
 src/soc/intel/skylake/acpi/pch.asl | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/skylake/acpi/pch.asl b/src/soc/intel/skylake/acpi/pch.asl
index ba9780881c..380ab1f0f5 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/skylake/acpi/pch.asl
+++ b/src/soc/intel/skylake/acpi/pch.asl
@@ -43,6 +43,9 @@
 /* USB XHCI 0:14.0 */
 #include "xhci.asl"
 
+/* Gigabit Ethernet 0:1f.6, with its wake capability */
+#include <soc/intel/common/block/acpi/acpi/pch_glan.asl>
+
 /* CSE/HECI #1 0:16.0 */
 #include <soc/intel/common/block/acpi/acpi/heci.asl>
 
